# Enforce LF line endings for all text files across every platform.
# Without this, Windows checkouts with `core.autocrlf=true` can present
# files as CRLF on disk, which makes Prettier's `prettier/prettier` rule
# flag every line — even though the file in the repo index is LF.
#
# `text=auto` lets Git detect text vs binary; `eol=lf` forces LF on both
# checkout and commit for detected text files.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Explicitly mark binaries so Git doesn't try to normalize them.
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf binary
*.otf binary
*.eot binary
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.icns binary
*.pdf binary
*.node binary
*.exe binary
*.dll binary
*.so binary
*.dylib binary
